Haili Hu, June 14 2017, SRON

-----------------------------------------
RemoTeC simulation package v2.4.8
----------------------------------------- 
  
Compilation:
------------
  Set compilation options in Makefile: 
  - parallel = yes / no    # no for creating synthetic spectra
  - debug = yes / no
  - FORT = SRON-ifort / SRON-gfortran / KIT-sun
  run "make"for main executables RemoTeC_create and RemoTeC_sim
  run "make create" for RemoTeC_create only
  run "make sim" for RemoTeC_sim only  
  
Use 'gmake' for compiling (in Debian it's called make).

If you run the code parallel, you need to increase the stacksize of threads 
by setting the environment variable OMP_STACKSIZE=40M. Increase the 
stacksize of the master threat with "ulimit -s unlimited". Depending on your 
system, the variable OMP_NUM_THREADS might need to be set.

Input data:
-----------
Input data (LUTs, solar model, etc) are not under version control and can be
downloaded elsewhere (location TBD). Every released version should have a 
corresponding tagged set of input data.
Set paths to input directories in namelist files in RUNDIR/INI/SRON/settings***.nml
 
Settings for creating synthetic measurements are set in RUNDIR/INI/synRUNID.nml, 
see for example RUNDIR/INI/SRON/syn.nml. If synRUNID.nml is missing default S5P 
settings will be used.

For an error sensitivity study, set errors in RUNDIR/INI/errorsRUNID.nml, see for 
example RUNDIR/INI/SRON/errors.nml If errorsRUNID.nml is missing no errors are 
applied.

Running and testing the code:
-----------------------------
Note that remotec_core can handle both scalar and vector RT. For the tests below, choose vector RT by: 
> cp SRC/remotec_core_vector/INCLUDES/parameter_scalar.inc SRC/remotec_core/INCLUDES/parameter.inc
IMPORTANT: do not put SRC/remotec_core/INCLUDES/parameter.inc in the repository, because then 
everytime somebody does a pull this file will be overwritten!

Generating synthetic measurements using old-style ascii atmospheric input:
> cd RUNDIR
> cp INI/SRON/settings_create_s5p_ensemble1.nml INI/settings0001.nml
>  ../RemoTeC_create 1 INI/test_atm_s5p_ensemble1
The generated spectra in SYNTH_SPECTRA can be compared to those in 
TEST/SYNTH_SPECTRA with TEST/test_ensemble1.gnu in gnuplot for example.

Retrieving synthetic measurements in old-style ascii format:
> cp INI/SRON/settings_retrieve_s5p_ensemble1.nml INI/settings0002.nml
> ../RemoTeC_sim 2 INI/test_spectra_s5p_ensemble1 > test2.out
> diffuse test2.out TEST/.
> diffuse CONTRL_OUT/statistics0002.dat TEST/.
Minor system-dependent differences may occur.

For a full test, run the entire ensemble and compare statistics.
-----------------------------
Generating synthetic measurements using MIPrep input (generating L1B in ascii and netCDF format):
> cd RUNDIR
> cp INI/SRON/syn_s5p_ensemble2_2win.nml INI/syn0003.nml
> cp INI/SRON/settings_create_s5p_ensemble2_2win.nml INI/settings0003.nml
>  ../RemoTeC_create 3 INI/test_atm_s5p_ensemble2

The generated spectra in SYNTH_SPECTRA can be compared to those in 
TEST/SYNTH_SPECTRA with TEST/test_ensemble2.gnu in gnuplot for example.

Retrieving synthetic measurements in ascii format:
> cp INI/SRON/settings_retrieve_s5p_ensemble2_ascii.nml INI/settings0004.nml
> ../RemoTeC_sim 4 INI/test_spectra_s5p_ensemble2 > test4.out
> diffuse test4.out TEST/.
> diffuse CONTRL_OUT/statistics0004.dat TEST/.

Retrieving synthetic measurements in netCDF format:
> cp INI/SRON/settings_retrieve_s5p_ensemble2_nc.nml INI/settings0005.nml
> ../RemoTeC_sim 5 INI/test_atm_s5p_ensemble2 > test5.out
> diffuse test5.out TEST/.
> diffuse CONTRL_OUT/statistics0005.dat TEST/.

Mercurial repositories:
-----------------------
The three source directories (remotec_core/, sim_retrieval/, sim_create/) 
are in subrepositories with the current directory as a thin shell main
repository. The subrepository remotec_core/ is also used in other
projects, e.g. GOSAT and S5P retrievals, thus project-specfic source files should 
not be placed here. Source files specific to the creating/retrieving spectra 
should be placed in sim_create/ and sim_retrieval/, respectively. 
